{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And she saw him, that he was good.</b> Because he was born at six months, as Rashi explained, she thought he was stillborn, and she checked his nails whether they were fully grown — which is a sign of viability. Immediately, ״ותרא אותו כי טוב הוא״ — that he had signs of viability, and therefore ״ותצפנהו״. Another interpretation: ״כי טוב הוא״ — he was beautiful, as in ״ונשבע לחם ונהיה טובים״, which means beautiful."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:29.553703092Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}